A||N||7||Slapnutz2000||White Gauges, 4x10 Speakers, Auto Shift Knob||||6||
Z||000000||Slapnutz2000||03-30-2000||01:04 PM||||Anyone have 86 2m4 notchback white gauges for $20? I've seen them on EBay but haven't seen them in while.<P>How long should it take to change the front dash speakers?<P>I also need a glossy black automatic shift knob. Know where I can find one?<P>Thanks everyone!<BR>James||||reg||6
Z||000001||ChadMan||03-30-2000||03:59 PM||||You should be able to change out your dash speakers in an hour or less.  The original factory speaker wires connect to the speakers using a molded clip (not standard blade connectors) so you'll have to cut the wires and connect them to your new speakers with crimp connectors or solder.<P>That's the most time-consuming part - removing and installing the speakers is a breeze.  One pry-off cover and four 7mm bolts per side and you're done!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||03-30-2000||09:24 PM||||The white, $20 gauge faces are just stickers.  Pretty generic looking IMHO.  I thought about that (for about 3 seconds!) then decided that I'd just wait until I had the money and get some backlit gauges and SXMs "real" gauge faces.||||reg||1
Z||000003||SloPonti||03-31-2000||12:45 AM||||here is a picture of the white gauges off of ebay! i bought them-figured what the heck=15 bucks no biggy! i think they look great=not cheap!!! it was easy to do! i reccommend them only for the 84 gauges that ARE NOT backlit! these will work perfect for us-besides the expensive white gauges are not available for us anyways!<BR>let me know your opinions of them!<BR>Rob <A HREF="http://members.aol.com/sloponti/gauge1.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://members.aol.com/sloponti/gauge1.jpg</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cooter||03-31-2000||12:56 AM||||I was wondering how those gauge stickers would look in red for my 85se. I may order up a set to see. <BR>SloPonti- did you have to remove the gauge needles to put on the stickers? If so, how hard was it?||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||03-31-2000||11:23 AM||||Those look better than I thought, but I'll still wait and get some backlit gauges and SXMs parts.||||reg||1
Z||000006||SloPonti||03-31-2000||07:35 PM||||yes i had to remove the needles from the gauges! they just pull right off! the guy who sells these gives you detail instructions on how to make your gauges! i did take mine and painted them white under the stickers-makes for a better final appearence!<BR>thank<BR>rob||||reg||1
Z||000007||Haze_Performance||04-02-2000||03:47 AM||||I got a set of the white face overlays off of ebay for one of my mustangs (86).  They arent to bad. I was going to get a set for my 85 2M4 but if you look at the gauges there are two small rivets on the faces. I dont know how well the overlay will stick to them. You may have small bumps that look like air bubbles.<p>[This message has been edited by Haze_Performance (edited 04-02-2000).]||||reg||13
